SEG = "LIC"
CAT = "fvicLicence"
Q = [
    ("Under s 17, the minimum age for an adult longarm licence in Victoria is:",
     "18 years", ["16 years", "17 years", "21 years"],
     "Section 17(1)(b) bars a longarm or handgun licence if the applicant is under 18. Younger shooters can apply for a junior licence from age 12."),
    ("The Chief Commissioner must not issue a first longarm licence until how long after the application?",
     "At least 28 days", ["At least 7 days", "At least 14 days", "At least 90 days"],
     "Section 33 says a licence under Part 2 must not be issued until at least 28 days have expired after the application was made."),
    ("Which of these is a genuine reason for a category A or B licence under s 10?",
     "Primary production", ["Self-defence at home", "Deterring burglars at home", "Keeping as an investment"],
     "Section 10(1) lists sport or target shooting, hunting, primary production, the occupation of security or prison guard, and official, commercial or prescribed purposes."),
    ("To use sport or target shooting as your genuine reason, you must be a member of:",
     "An approved shooting club", ["Any registered sporting body", "A firearms dealer's mailing list", "A local council sports club"],
     "Section 10(2)(a) requires membership of a shooting club or organisation approved by the Chief Commissioner, and shooting only at an authorised place."),
    ("Which document can support hunting as your genuine reason under s 10(2)(b)?",
     "Your current Game Licence", ["Your recreational fishing licence", "Your current driver licence", "Your marine boat licence"],
     "Section 10(2)(b) accepts a Game Licence under the Wildlife Act 1975, written evidence of land you own or manage, written permission from a private landholder, approved club membership, or a pest-shooting engagement."),
    ("A hunter relying on someone else's farm for a genuine reason must produce:",
     "The owner's written permission", ["A verbal promise by phone", "A neighbour's statutory declaration", "The farm's council rates notice"],
     "Section 10(2)(b)(ii) requires written evidence from the owner or manager of privately owned land that you may use it for hunting from time to time."),
    ("Besides a genuine reason, s 17 requires an applicant to have completed an approved firearms safety course and to have:",
     "A good knowledge of firearms law", ["Owned a firearm in the past", "A club referee's written report", "A shooting range accuracy score"],
     "Section 17(1)(c)(iii) requires satisfactory completion of a course of firearms safety approved by the Chief Commissioner and a good knowledge of firearms law."),
    ("Under s 17, a licence will not be issued unless the applicant can comply with:",
     "The storage requirements", ["A minimum income level", "A fitness standard", "A shooting accuracy test"],
     "Section 17(1)(c)(iv) requires the Chief Commissioner to be satisfied the applicant can comply with the storage requirements set out by or under the Act."),
    ("A person who does not ordinarily live in Victoria can be issued a Victorian licence if they:",
     "Need it for work in Victoria", ["Own a holiday home there", "Visit for a hunting trip", "Hold a Victorian driver licence"],
     "Section 17(1)(ab) bars an applicant not ordinarily resident in Victoria unless the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the licence is needed for work purposes in Victoria."),
    ("A category A or B longarm licence lasts for the period specified in it, but no longer than:",
     "5 years", ["2 years", "3 years", "10 years"],
     "Section 39(1) sets a maximum of 5 years from issue or renewal for licences other than category C, D or E and junior licences."),
    ("A category C longarm licence lasts no longer than:",
     "3 years", ["1 year", "5 years", "10 years"],
     "Section 39(2) limits category C, D and E longarm licences to a period not exceeding 3 years from issue or renewal."),
    ("A junior licence holder turning 18 keeps the junior licence in force if, before their birthday, they:",
     "Apply for an adult licence", ["Join a second shooting club", "Tell their school in writing", "Buy their own category A rifle"],
     "Section 39A keeps a junior licence in force after the holder turns 18 if, before then, the holder applied for a licence for the same category of firearms."),
    ("Your renewal application is still being decided on the day your licence expires. The licence:",
     "Continues until it is decided", ["Ends at midnight that day", "Ends after a 7-day grace period", "Ends if you own a firearm"],
     "Section 41A deems a licence to continue in force from its expiry date until the renewal application is determined, as long as you applied before it expired."),
    ("You decide not to renew your licence. The Firearm Safety Code booklet says that before it expires you must:",
     "Dispose of them to a dealer", ["Lend them to a licensed friend", "Lock them in a relative's safe", "Remove the bolts and keep them"],
     "The booklet says that if you do not intend to renew, you must dispose of your firearms to a licensed firearms dealer before the licence expires, or face penalties."),
    ("Under the general conditions in Schedule 1, a licence holder must allow a police officer to:",
     "Inspect your storage when reasonable", ["Test fire the firearm at any time", "Keep a spare key to the safe", "Search the whole house each month"],
     "Schedule 1 item 1 requires the holder to permit a police officer to inspect the holder's storage arrangements at any reasonable time."),
    ("Schedule 1 says a licence holder must not do what with the licence itself?",
     "Lend it to another person", ["Carry it in a wallet", "Show it to a dealer", "Keep a copy at home"],
     "Schedule 1 item 2 says the holder must not transfer, lend or give the licence to another person."),
    ("The reason you hold your licence changes. Under Schedule 1, you must tell the Chief Commissioner within:",
     "7 days", ["24 hours", "14 days", "28 days"],
     "Schedule 1 item 4 requires notice of any change to the reason for which the licence was issued within 7 days of becoming aware of the change."),
    ("A person becomes the respondent to a final family violence intervention order. They are a prohibited person for:",
     "The order and 5 years after", ["The order's term only", "12 months after the order ends", "Life, with no review possible"],
     "Victoria Police says a final intervention order makes the respondent prohibited for the duration of the order and five years after it expires, unless a court deems them non-prohibited."),
    ("According to Victoria Police, the respondent to an interim intervention order is generally:",
     "Not a prohibited person", ["Prohibited for 5 years", "Prohibited for life", "Prohibited for 12 months"],
     "Victoria Police says a respondent to an interim intervention order is not considered a prohibited person unless the order contains conditions about firearms, such as suspension or surrender."),
    ("When the Chief Commissioner learns a licence holder has become a prohibited person, s 46 says the licence:",
     "Must be cancelled at once", ["Lapses at the next renewal", "Is reviewed by a magistrate", "Is limited to category A"],
     "Section 46(1) requires the Chief Commissioner to cancel the licence immediately on becoming aware the holder is a prohibited person."),
    ("Police serve a suspension notice on you in person. Under s 53, you must surrender your firearms and licence:",
     "Immediately to that person", ["Within 7 days to a police station", "Within 28 days to a dealer", "At your next renewal"],
     "Section 53(1)(a) requires immediate surrender to the person serving the notice when served personally. If the notice comes by post, the surrender is within 7 days at a police station."),
    ("A suspension notice arrives by post. Under s 53, you have how long to surrender your firearms at a police station?",
     "7 days", ["24 hours", "14 days", "28 days"],
     "Section 53(1)(b) allows 7 days after service by post to surrender any firearm, ammunition and the licence document to a police station."),
    ("When the Chief Commissioner suspends a licence and proposes to cancel it, the holder may make written submissions within:",
     "28 days", ["7 days", "14 days", "3 months"],
     "Section 47(3)(d) says the suspension notice must state that written submissions may be made within 28 days of the notice."),
    ("A junior licence application must be made with the written consent of:",
     "A parent or guardian", ["The applicant's school principal", "A licensed firearms dealer", "The junior's club coach"],
     "Section 20(1)(c) bars a junior licence unless the application is made with the written consent of a person with parental responsibility for the applicant."),
    ("A hunting licence holder wants to shoot on a neighbour's paddock. Schedule 2 says that before entering, they must get permission from:",
     "The owner or occupier", ["The local council", "A police officer", "The Game Management Authority"],
     "Schedule 2 item 1(1) makes it a licence condition that the holder gets the permission of the owner or occupier before entering privately owned land to hunt."),
    ("A primary producer licensed for category A wants to shoot on another farmer's property. Schedule 2 allows this with:",
     "That landowner's permission", ["A permit from the council", "No permission at all", "A Game Licence only"],
     "Schedule 2 item 1(7) authorises a primary production licence holder to carry or use the licensed longarm on another primary producer's land with the owner's permission."),
    ("A clay target shooter holding a category C licence must take part in how many clay competitions each calendar year?",
     "At least 4", ["At least 2", "At least 6", "At least 12"],
     "Schedule 2 item 2(2)(b) requires at least 4 clay target competitions a calendar year, conducted by clay target clubs or organisations, plus continuing club membership."),
    ("According to Victoria Police, a person prohibited because of criminal offending may stay prohibited for up to:",
     "15 years after prison", ["5 years after prison", "10 years after the offence", "2 years after the court case"],
     "Victoria Police says prohibition for criminal offending can last from 12 months after a finding of guilt up to 15 years after serving a term of imprisonment, as set out in s 3."),
]
